# vtb.R -- VTB United League wrappers over two keyless public JSON backends of vtb-league.com, at parity with
# sdv-py sportsdataverse/basketball/vtb (origin/main e3d232ebc9): api.vtb-league.com/v2 (vtb_league_*, the
# schedule API) and Infobasket, the Russian basketball federation's stats platform (org.infobasket.su,
# vtb_infobasket_*). Transport, season mapping, personal-data scrub and refusals: R/vtb_runtime.R; frames:
# R/vtb_parsers.R; columns and code tables: R/vtb_tables.R. Generated by a scratch generator from the sdv-py
# endpoint YAMLs, returns schemas and manual_column_descriptions.yaml; regenerate rather than hand-edit.

# The @details of every vtb topic that shares the vtb_infobasket_seasons() notes (roxygen @eval .intl_details()).
.vtb_infobasket_seasons_details <- c(
  "* Owner flag (sdv-internal-refs/vtb/README.md): the VTB United League is run from Russia and several clubs are owned",
  "  or sponsored by sanctioned state companies (the KHL precedent); Infobasket is the Russian basketball federation's",
  "  stats platform. Fetching on your own machine is fine. The owner has approved published data releases (2026-10-17),",
  "  though none is scheduled yet. No accounts or payments are involved.",
  "* Unofficial and unsupported: both hosts are keyless public JSON backends of vtb-league.com. No terms of use are",
  "  published; robots.txt is a 404 on api.vtb-league.com and org.infobasket.su (no rules; vtb-league.com disallows",
  "  only /wp/wp-admin/). The runtime waits at least 1 s before every request, retries included, and honours",
  "  Retry-After on 429 / 503. No key, cookie or proxy is used (live-verified direct from the droplet 2026-10-12).",
  "* Seasons are END years (2026 = 2025-26) on both backends. Infobasket keys everything by competition id:",
  "  vtb_infobasket_seasons maps the END year to the season-level CompID, and the season-keyed wrappers do that mapping",
  "  for you. CompID means three things: a season (50714), a stage below it (50720 regular season, 54281 playoff;",
  "  stage-level wrappers take the stage id from vtb_infobasket_comp_issue) and, in the player season stats, an END",
  "  year.",
  "* Ids: the v2 matchId is the Infobasket GameID, the v2 teamId the Infobasket TeamID and the v2 venueId the",
  "  Infobasket ArenaId. team_id is the key on every team route; comp_team_id (a registration in one stage) and the",
  "  club-record id of the team page are other key spaces. person_id is one person across clubs and seasons.",
  "* Errors are HTTP 200: an unknown id answers \\{MessageType, Message\\}, an unknown game the string 'BadRequest'; both",
  "  are `hoopR_asset_fetch` (a failed fetch), never an empty frame. A body for another game, person, team, competition",
  "  or season than the one asked for is `hoopR_asset_fetch` too, as is a game that is not final (box score, plays and",
  "  header need GameStatus 1) and a partial GetTeamStats page. An empty list is `hoopR_no_data`.",
  "* Coverage: calendars and box scores from 2009-10; play-by-play and shot x/y from 2022-23 only (earlier games give",
  "  an empty pbp frame), officials in the line-ups from 2022-23. Shot x/y are decimetres from the basket centre",
  "  (orientation unverified). Counting statistics are null instead of 0 on the wire (the parsers fill 0), percentages",
  "  and averages are comma-decimal strings (the parsers return floats), the paint statistics are broken and dropped,",
  "  and dates come in three encodings (the parsers return ISO strings; .NET instants as Moscow time with its +03:00",
  "  offset).",
  "* Personal data: the runtime removes licence numbers, contact and operator-account fields for everyone and the birth",
  "  dates, birth years and ages of coaches, referees and other officials from every body. Players' public bio (birth",
  "  date, height, weight, nationality) is kept.",
  "* Other tags (vtbyouth, wbc, wpremier, rfb) answer through the tag argument; only vtb was captured. The team routes",
  "  key on the END-year season (sdv-py also lets a caller pass a stage CompID through params; the R wrappers do not).",
  "* Errors are classed conditions, all inheriting `hoopR_error`: `hoopR_no_data` (HTTP 404, or the host has nothing",
  "  for the request: an empty list, a v2 season with no rows, a season without team totals), `hoopR_bad_request` (a",
  "  malformed id or league slug, a lang other than en or ru, or a season the competition tag does not have) and",
  "  `hoopR_asset_fetch` (any other non-2xx, an empty or non-JSON body, an error envelope or string, a game that is not",
  "  final or a stub, a partial or possibly truncated page, or a body for another game, person, team, competition,",
  "  league or season). HTTP 500 is retried (neither host answers 500 for an unknown id). Wrappers raise; they never",
  "  warn and return empty."
)

#' @title
#' **Get VTB Infobasket Seasons**
#' @description
#' Season END year -> season-level CompID for a competition tag (the table every season-keyed wrapper maps with).
#'
#' Endpoint: `GET https://org.infobasket.su/Comp/GetSeasonsForTag`
#' @param tag Competition tag scoping the profile: vtb (VTB United League, default), vtbyouth, wbc, wpremier or rfb.
#'   The season table is read for this tag.
#' @return
#' A `hoopR_data` tibble: Season END year -> season-level CompID for a competition tag (the table every season-keyed
#'   wrapper maps with). The columns are always these, in this order (sdv-py `vtb_infobasket_seasons`); an empty valid
#'   answer raises `hoopR_no_data`, a valid body with no rows for this frame is a zero-row tibble:
#'
#' | col_name | type | description |
#' |:---|:---|:---|
#' | season | integer | Season END year (2026 = 2025-26): the season the request asked for, stamped by the runtime. |
#' | comp_id | integer | Season-level CompID of that season (50714 = VTB 2025-26). Pass it as `comps` to /Comp/GetCalendar/. |
#' | name_ru | character | Season name in Russian ('Sezon 2025/2026' = 'Season 2025/2026'). |
#' | name_en | character | Season name in English. |
#' | db | character | Infobasket database the competition lives in ('org'). |
#' | tag | character | Competition tag of the request (vtb is the VTB United League; vtbyouth, wbc, wpremier and rfb also answer). |
#' @eval .intl_details(.vtb_infobasket_seasons_details)
#' @examples
#' \donttest{
#'   try(vtb_infobasket_seasons())
#' }
#' @export
#' @family VTB Functions
vtb_infobasket_seasons <- function(tag = "vtb") {
  withr::local_options(list(scipen = 999, stringsAsFactors = FALSE))
  call <- rlang::current_env()
  raw <- .vtb_ib_get("/Comp/GetSeasonsForTag", ids = list(), query = list(format = "json", tag = tag), call = call)
  .vtb_out("vtb_infobasket_seasons", raw, "VTB Infobasket Seasons from org.infobasket.su")
}

#' @title
#' **Get VTB Infobasket Calendar**
#' @description
#' Every game of a season (finished, live and planned): teams, scores, date, venue, attendance.
#'
#' Endpoint: `GET https://org.infobasket.su/Comp/GetCalendar/`
#' @param season Season END year (2026 = 2025-26); the wrapper maps it to the season-level Infobasket CompID with
#'   vtb_infobasket_seasons (one extra request per tag, cached). Required.
#' @param tag Competition tag scoping the profile: vtb (VTB United League, default), vtbyouth, wbc, wpremier or rfb.
#'   The season table is read for this tag.
#' @return
#' A `hoopR_data` tibble: Every game of a season (finished, live and planned): teams, scores, date, venue, attendance.
#'   The columns are always these, in this order (sdv-py `vtb_infobasket_calendar`); an empty valid answer raises
#'   `hoopR_no_data`, a valid body with no rows for this frame is a zero-row tibble:
#'
#' | col_name | type | description |
#' |:---|:---|:---|
#' | season | integer | Season END year (2026 = 2025-26): the season the request asked for, stamped by the runtime. |
#' | comp_id | integer | Season-level Infobasket CompID of the season (50714 = 2025-26): the id every season-keyed route takes. |
#' | game_id | integer | Infobasket game id (GameID); equals the v2 API `matchId`. Joins to /Widget/GetOnline/\{gameId\} and /Widget/GamePage/\{gameId\}. |
#' | game_number | character | Game number within the competition, e.g. 'RS-002' (RS = regular season); playoff games use the series code. |
#' | game_date | character | Game date as an ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD); the wire sends DD.MM.YYYY. |
#' | has_time | logical | True when a tip-off time is set. |
#' | game_time | character | Tip-off local time, 'HH:MM'. |
#' | game_time_msk | character | Tip-off time in Moscow time ('HH:MM' on calendar rows, 'HH.MM' in GetOnline). |
#' | game_date_time | character | Tip-off instant as an ISO 8601 string in Moscow time with its +03:00 offset (the wire sends a .NET /Date(ms)/ value). |
#' | game_date_time_moscow | character | Tip-off instant as an ISO 8601 string in Moscow time with its +03:00 offset (the wire's second .NET date; equal to game_date_time in every sample). |
#' | game_status | integer | Game status in the calendar code set: 0 planned, 1 completed, 2 live. |
#' | team_a_id | integer | Team A (home) TeamID. Infobasket team id (TeamID): one club's entry in a competition family (Lokomotiv Kuban = 2650). Joins to /Widget/Team*/\{teamId\} and equals the v2 API `teamId`. |
#' | team_b_id | integer | Team B (away) TeamID. Infobasket team id (TeamID): one club's entry in a competition family (Lokomotiv Kuban = 2650). Joins to /Widget/Team*/\{teamId\} and equals the v2 API `teamId`. |
#' | short_team_name_aru | character | Team short name of team A (home), Russian. |
#' | short_team_name_bru | character | Team short name of team B (away), Russian. |
#' | team_name_aru | character | Team name with city in brackets of team A (home), Russian. |
#' | team_name_bru | character | Team name with city in brackets of team B (away), Russian. |
#' | comp_team_name_aru | character | Team name as registered in the competition of team A (home), Russian. |
#' | comp_team_name_bru | character | Team name as registered in the competition of team B (away), Russian. |
#' | region_team_name_aru | character | Team's city or region of team A (home), Russian. |
#' | region_team_name_bru | character | Team's city or region of team B (away), Russian. |
#' | short_team_name_aen | character | Team short name of team A (home), English. |
#' | short_team_name_ben | character | Team short name of team B (away), English. |
#' | team_name_aen | character | Team name with city in brackets of team A (home), English. |
#' | team_name_ben | character | Team name with city in brackets of team B (away), English. |
#' | comp_team_name_aen | character | Team name as registered in the competition of team A (home), English. |
#' | comp_team_name_ben | character | Team name as registered in the competition of team B (away), English. |
#' | region_team_name_aen | character | Team's city or region of team A (home), English. |
#' | region_team_name_ben | character | Team's city or region of team B (away), English. |
#' | score_a | integer | Final score of team A (home). |
#' | score_b | integer | Final score of team B (away). |
#' | tv_ru | character | TV channels, in Russian. |
#' | tv_en | character | TV channels, in English. |
#' | region_ru | character | City or region of the game's venue in Russian. |
#' | region_en | character | City or region of the game's venue in English. |
#' | arena_en | character | Arena name, English. |
#' | arena_ru | character | Arena, Russian ('SK' = sports complex). |
#' | arena_id | integer | Infobasket arena id; equals the v2 API `venueId` (11687 = SK Basket-Hall, Krasnodar). |
#' | game_attendance | integer | Spectators at the game (null when not recorded). |
#' | comp_name_ru | character | Stage name, Russian ('Regulyarnyy chempionat' = 'Regular Season', 'Gruppa A' = 'Group A'). |
#' | comp_name_en | character | Stage name (e.g. 'Regular Season'), English. |
#' | league_name_ru | character | League name, Russian ('Edinaya liga VTB' / 'Chempionat Edinoy ligi VTB' = 'VTB United League' / 'VTB United League Championship'). |
#' | league_name_en | character | League name, English. |
#' | league_short_name_ru | character | League short name, Russian ('VTB' = 'VTB'). |
#' | league_short_name_en | character | League short name, English. |
#' | gender | integer | Competition gender: 0 on every VTB sample (men). Other values unverified. |
#' @inherit vtb_infobasket_seasons details
#' @examples
#' \donttest{
#'   try(vtb_infobasket_calendar(season = 2026))
#' }
#' @export
#' @family VTB Functions
vtb_infobasket_calendar <- function(season, tag = "vtb") {
  withr::local_options(list(scipen = 999, stringsAsFactors = FALSE))
  call <- rlang::current_env()
  raw <- .vtb_ib_get(
    "/Comp/GetCalendar/", ids = list(),
    query = list(format = "json", season = season, tag = tag),
    call = call
  )
  .vtb_out("vtb_infobasket_calendar", raw, "VTB Infobasket Calendar from org.infobasket.su")
}

#' @title
